$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041946/state.json" "file_sha256" "89c26bb53c7ff8dec2509721ddcd5b67128bb5dccc5f11da899be7e67c7e43d2" "basis" 1541 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041946/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-20600" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 18 & 380 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 9 & 190 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 19\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that the matrix $M$ is already in row echelon form.\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 18 & 380 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 9 & 190 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 19\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-9){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 18 & 380 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 19 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 19\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-18){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 38 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 19 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 19\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 76 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 19 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 19\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041946/state.json" "file_sha256" "89c26bb53c7ff8dec2509721ddcd5b67128bb5dccc5f11da899be7e67c7e43d2" "basis" 1541 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041946/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-20600" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041946/act