cation.json"} {"question" "q-10636" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,0,0⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041946/state.json" "file_sha256" "89c26bb53c7ff8dec2509721ddcd5b67128bb5dccc5f11da899be7e67c7e43d2" "basis" 1541 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041946/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74629" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-4x-12y+12z=-4 \\\\ 5x+16y-9z=4 \\\\ 2x+6y-6z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041946/state.json" "file_sha256" "89c26bb53c7ff8dec2509721ddcd5b67128bb5dccc5f11da899be7e67c7e43d2" "basis" 1541 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041946/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74629" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -12 & 12 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 16 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ into reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -12 & 12 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 16 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=(-\\frac{1}{4}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 16 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the row echelon form above, we have only two pivots (in the $1$st and $2$nd columns). To transform the matrix to reduced row echelon form, we need to create zeros above the pivots only. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -21 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-21z=4 \\\\ y+6z=-1 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final equation, we can remove this equation from the system. \n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=21z+4 \\\\ y=-6z-1 \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}21z+4 \\\\ -6z-1 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041946/state.json" "file_sha256" "89c26bb53c7ff8dec2509721ddcd5b67128bb5dccc5f11da899be7e67c7e43d2" "basis" 1541 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041946/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74629" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041946/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1990a03c31fd02ecd326c98c9804681ab3c0586325b05a4a600d78af760dd769" "basis" 1541 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041946/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74629" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041946/state.json" "file_sha256" "89c26bb53c7ff8dec2509721ddcd5b67128bb5dccc5f11da899be7e67c7e43d2" "basis" 1541 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041946/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74629" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}21z+4 \\\\ -6z-1 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041946/state.json" "file_sha256" "89c26bb53c7ff8dec2509721ddcd5b67128bb5dccc5f11da899be7e67c7e43d2" "basis" 1541 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041946/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74629" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}21z+4 \\\\ 6z-1 \\\\ z-2\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041946/state.json" "file_sha256" "89c26bb53c7ff8dec2509721ddcd5b67128bb5dccc5f11da899be7e67c7e43d2" "basis" 1541 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041946/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74629" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\beg