cc5f11da899be7e67c7e43d2" "basis" 1541 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041946/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74612" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-10y-5z=10 \\\\ -10x+100y+50z=-100 \\\\ -4x+40y+20z=-40\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041946/state.json" "file_sha256" "89c26bb53c7ff8dec2509721ddcd5b67128bb5dccc5f11da899be7e67c7e43d2" "basis" 1541 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041946/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74612" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 & -5 & 10 \\\\ -10 & 100 & 50 & -100 \\\\ -4 & 40 & 20 & -40\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 & -5 & 10 \\\\ -10 & 100 & 50 & -100 \\\\ -4 & 40 & 20 & -40\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+10{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 40 & 20 & -40\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041946/state.json" "file_sha256" "89c26bb53c7ff8dec2509721ddcd5b67128bb5dccc5f11da899be7e67c7e43d2" "basis" 1541 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041946/edb-import/verification.json"} {