a_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079061/state.json" "file_sha256" "bea1219838bc2a0c90cd431ccbac16a30fa75e03d3fcfdc1265d91b3e1b59253"} {"question" "q-20597" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that the matrix $M$ is already in row echelon form.\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+3{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x=2 \\\\  & y=4 \\\\  & z=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have he solution $x=2$, $y=4$ and $z=-2.$ Or, in vector form $⟨2,4,-2⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079061/state.json" "file_sha256" "bea1219838bc2a0c90cd431ccbac16a30fa75e03d3fcfdc1265d91b3e1b59253"} {"question" "q-20597" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079061/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8ebf2f6de173fc8bd7ea752d048f2f6dff5564dc1ba4ce9f8594cac88eae1cd7"} {"question" "q-20597" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/1407